cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.
title: >-
  Subject-independent decoding of attended spatial location from fNIRS:
  analysis code
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and results for a study of subject-independent decoding of
  attended spatial location from functional near-infrared spectroscopy, using
  the public OpenNeuro datasets ds004830 (twelve participants, three talker
  locations) and ds007738 (twenty-nine participants, two locations, with
  covert-attention and eye-movement-only tasks). The code evaluates decoders
  trained on all but one participant and tested on the participant left out,
  under causal (past-trials-only) and transductive (whole-recording) feature
  normalisation, measures calibration curves as the new participant contributes
  labelled trials, and tests how much of the transferable signal is shared with
  eye movement. The datasets themselves are not redistributed here.
